<title>USA: Partial U.S. House election results as of 1631 GMT.</title>
<headline>Partial U.S. House election results as of 1631 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are election results of 65 of the most competitive U.S. House of Representatives races according to projections by major news organisations as of 11:31 a.m. EST (1631 GMT).</p>
<p>In the previous Congress, the Republicans had a 235-197 majority in the House with one independent and two vacancies.</p>
<p>Democrats needed a minimum gain of 19 seats to recapture control of the House.</p>
<p>These closely-watched races represent only about 15 percent of the 435 House races, but are meant as a guide to the election trend.</p>
